==Battleground==
*2 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*3 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Fallen Bear]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Kappy Kawano]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**5 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Zoge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**2 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Kappy Kawano is quite the threatening beast, and this stage's support doesn't help either. Your standard [[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Surge-immune]] combo of [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] + Talented [[Actress Cat (Special Cat)|Beefcake Cat]] + Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] should be enough to take out Kawano eventually, as well as the Miz Devils. Other helpful units include [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] as a meatshield unaffected by [[Surge Attack|Surges]], a [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]] to hinder the Fallen Bear (though with his low strength magnification you can easily brute-force his [[Shield]]), and a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] if you end up struggling against the Zigges. Stacking [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cats]] is also an option if you feel like it.

Unlike in [[Kappy Jr.]]'s stages, [[Brainwashed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed UFO/Flying Cat]] can actually be used thanks to Kawano's slow attack rate and minimal support.

==Trivia==
*"Ghost" is a translation of 妖怪 ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'', a class of supernatural creatures and phenomena in Japanese folklore. The ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'' is an example of a ''yōkai''.

